# * check accounts
# ** 1. check accounts succeeds when all accounts are declared
<
account a
2020-01-01
  (a)  1
$ hledger -f- check accounts

# ** 2. and otherwise fails:
<
2020-01-01
  (a)  1
$ hledger -f- check accounts
>2 /account "a" has not been declared/
>=1

# ** 3. also fails for forecast accounts
<
commodity $
account a
~ 2022-01-31
    a  $1
    b

$ hledger -f- --today 2022-01-01 --forecast check accounts
>2 /account "b" has not been declared/
>=1

# ** 4. also fails in --strict mode
$ hledger -f- --today 2022-01-01 --forecast --strict bal
>2 /account "b" has not been declared/
>=1

# ** 5. also fails for auto accounts
<
commodity $
account a

= a
  (b)    $1

2022-01-31
    (a)  $1

2022-02-01
$ hledger -f- --auto check accounts
>2 /account "b" has not been declared/
>=1

# ** 6. also fails in --strict mode
$ hledger -f- --auto --strict bal
>2 /account "b" has not been declared/
>=1

# ** 7. Accounts chosen by hledger for the postings it generates need not be declared:
# equity conversion postings (--infer-equity), gain postings, and imbalance postings (--infer-imbalance).
<
account assets:usd
account assets:chf
account assets:broker
account assets:cash
commodity AAPL  ; lots:

2024-01-30 exchange
    assets:usd   -19110.17 USD @ 0.869050 CHF
    assets:chf    16607.69 CHF

2026-01-01 buy
    assets:broker   3 AAPL {$33.33}
    assets:cash   $-99.99

2026-02-01 sell
    assets:broker   -3 AAPL @ $40.003
    assets:cash   $120.01

$ hledger -f- check accounts --infer-equity --infer-imbalance

# ** 8. But postings written by the user to those accounts are checked as usual.
<
account a

2024-01-01
    a                  1
    equity:imbalance  -1

$ hledger -f- check accounts --infer-imbalance
>2 /account "equity:imbalance" has not been declared/
>=1
